Z||000000||Fiero5||08-27-2001||12:12 AM||||You know what would be cool?<BR>Take a bunch of the awesome photo's that we see all the time on here of members rides, and have the photo's published in a Fiero photo book. We could do the sections by years. Show an original stock model for that year, then a bunch of the original ads Pontiac advertised for it for that year. Then show Pennocks members rides of that year. Each section could be another year, etc. Then do a section on kit's for Lambos and such.<BR>It could include specs and bios on each car and it's owner.<P>We could have a preface written by Cliff including info and a pic on his awesome Fiero.<P>I can line up a publisher, and then we can have each Pennocks member who would like to have their Fiero(s) published e-mail pics and the info to the publisher, or mail them if that works better.<P>Anyone interested?<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Glowing_Fiero9_sig.jpg">          <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||7
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-27-2001||02:15 AM||||I posted a similar idea this a month ago...good amount of interest.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009346.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009346.html</A> <P><BR>I have almost finished the online info submission form to be filled out about the owner/car.<P>Do you want to collaborate?  I have been offered help by other PFF members...I would appreciate it!  I like your ideas!<P>Haze_perf also had an idea for a book.<P>I am very serious about it and hope to be able to make the first run in September.<P>Joe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||08-27-2001||05:14 PM||||Sounds good. If we band together, we should be able to get alot more accomplished faster. My idea was to get enough members to respond to the post, so I could show a publisher the thread to show them the interest. Car books generally focus on a specialized audience, so you really have to show them the audience and sales potential to help them justify the cost of production.<P>The more info, pics and so forth, the better chance for a bigger/wider audience for your book.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Glowing_Fiero9_sig.jpg">          <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||7
Z||000003||Joe Torma||08-27-2001||07:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>The more info, pics and so forth, the better chance for a bigger/wider audience for your book.<P>Steve<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><u>OUR</u> book!<BR>I can handle the printing end of things. there are a lot of issues that a big time publisher won't want to deal with, mainly, the digitally submitted photos--and it is too time consuming and inefficient to scan 1000 photos in, when I can take any image on this forum and make them look good.<P>Do you glance at the other thread?  Do you like the binder idea?  IMO, its probably the best way to issue updates and still have everything as one book.<P>Where are you MinnGreen?  Still want to help?<P>Lets get this started!<P>||||reg||1
